# Tome of the Dead CONCEPT round-4 COMMON structure tiles (12 ids) — DRAFT. Supersedes walls.tiles
# (round-2 plaster) and walls_r3.tiles (round-3 whole-wall dither).
# Format = tools/gfx_convert.py --mode tile. Style brief (user ref assets/gfx/concept/ref/bloodstone.png,
# translated, not copied): mostly black, bricks as open OUTLINES (mortar only, = the existing WALL),
# architecture as crumbling FRAGMENTS with ragged edges, lumpy pillars, white rubble, cyan roots.
# Ink shown is the default; walls/pillars take ATTR_WALL[depth], platform_hi ATTR_FLOOR[depth].
# wall_worn        : WALL with broken mortar runs (variety inside a fragment)
# wall_brk_top/bot : a fragment's ragged top / bottom edge, bricks closed along the break,
#                    in register with WALL (rows 0/4 mortar), so they stack on WALL directly
# wall_brk_l/r     : ragged left / right edge of a fragment
# pillar_l/r       : lumpy organic pillar, 2 cols, repeats every 8 rows (open outline)
# platform_hi      : floor-row variant: highlight lip on top + broken brick lines (floor attr)
# rubble           : small pile on the standing row ($07)
# root_top/end1/end2: hanging roots ($05); end1<->end2 = 1-cell glyph-swap sway (optional)
